      <div type="clause" n="52.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 52.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="520" ed="#liebermann"/>E si l'un chalange le seignour, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.3"/> per li<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.4"/> s'ent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.5"/> seit alé, si s'escundie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.6"/> sei VI. main, e s'il ne pot, envers l[e<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.7"/>] rei l'ament. E cil<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.8"/> soit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.9"/> utlage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.a"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.10"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="520" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si calumpnietur, quod per eum fugerit, aut purget se manu sexta aut erga regem emendet. Et is qui fugerit, uthlagetur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="52.2" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="274" ed="#robertson"/>E si l'un chalange le seignour que per li s'ent seit alé, si s'escundie sei VI main, e s'il ne pot, envers l[e] rei l'ament. E cil soit utlage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="520" ed="#liebermann"/>52, 2. Und wenn man den Herrn anklagt, dass durch ihn jener davongegangen sei, so reinige er sich selbsechster Hand; und wenn er das nicht kann, büsse er es gegenüber dem König. Und jener sei friedlos (werde geächtet <hi rend="italic">L</hi>).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">52, 2. And if one accuses the lord that that man has gone away through him, then he shall clear himself with himself as sixth hand; and if he cannot do that, he shall pay compensation for it to the king. And that man shall be outlawed (be proscribed <hi rend="italic">L</hi>).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="275" ed="#robertson"/>And if the lord is accused of being an accessory to his flight, he shall clear himself with 5 compurgators, and if he cannot, he shall pay compensation to the king; and the man shall be an outlaw.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="520"><ref target="clause:IICn_31-1a">II Cn 31.1a</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_31-2">II Cn 31.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 31, 1a | ebd. 31, 2</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 274–275 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 520, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">520</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">utlagé <hi rend="italic">MAT., wie auch L ein Verbum hat; allein vielleicht ist Cnut's Adjectiv</hi> (utlage <hi rend="italic">Hs. A</hi>) <hi rend="italic">gemeint</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">utlagé MAT., as L too has a verb; but perhaps Cnut’s adjective (utlage MS A) is meant</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">520</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">520</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">le <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">le Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">520</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seut <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> sen <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seut Io; sen Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">520</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">escuudie <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">escuudie Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">520</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">li <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">li I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">520</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sil <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sil Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">520</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seit <hi rend="italic">bessert MA.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seit emended by MA.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52-2.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">520</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">endet Io;</hi> Attuli etiam mecum tunc de Londoniis copiam decisionis totius controuersiae inter Cant. ecclesiam et Eborac. . . . . a. 1072 <hi rend="italic">fährt fort Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Io ends; Im continues: Attuli etiam mecum tunc de Londoniis copiam decisionis totius controuersiae inter Cant. ecclesiam et Eborac. . . . . a. 1072</seg></note>
      </div>
